(LST-64 — `is not a` negates the predicate.
 Also covers: LST-66 (on a statically-typed value the predicate folds at
 compile time and is always true, so the sentence is legal on any value, not
 just a mixed one).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST-64.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   a number
   not a number
   not a number
   static number folds true
   static text folds true
)
a list called mixedbag is [1, "two", 3.5].
For each item in mixedbag,
  if item is not a number, print "not a number". otherwise print "a number".

a number called plain is 7.
if plain is a number then, print "static number folds true". otherwise print "static number folds false".
a text called label is "hi".
if label is a text then, print "static text folds true". otherwise print "static text folds false".
